{
  "$comment": [
    "Conformance cases for partner webhook verification. THIS FILE IS SHARED:",
    "vairified.js and vairified.py each run every case in their own test suite,",
    "in their own CI. A behaviour difference between the two SDKs therefore fails",
    "a build rather than waiting for somebody to notice.",
    "",
    "It exists because parity used to be a claim someone made after running an",
    "ad-hoc script, and that claim was wrong twice: a first pass said 13 of 13",
    "cases agreed, a review then found 14 more that all diverged, and a third",
    "pass found 15 real divergences in 41 cases. Fixing the named instances was",
    "not converging, so the mechanism changed.",
    "",
    "Bodies are hex so neither language builds its own input -- that is what",
    "makes the byte-level cases (BOM, invalid UTF-8) expressible at all.",
    "",
    "ADDING A CASE: add it here, in BOTH repos, byte-identical. If a reviewer",
    "finds a divergence, the fix is a case here, not a bug report.",
    "",
    "Expectations were produced by running vairified.js and are asserted by both",
    "SDKs. Changing one to make a build pass is a visible, reviewable diff."
  ],
